[{"category":"section","location":"91-api-delay/#api-delay","page":"Flight delay model","text":"Reference for the FlightDelayModel module, which samples root delay scenarios, propagates delays through a schedule and computes the resulting delay cost.","title":"Flight delay model"},{"category":"section","location":"91-api-delay/#Contents","page":"Flight delay model","text":"Pages = [\"91-api-delay.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"91-api-delay/#Index","page":"Flight delay model","text":"Pages = [\"91-api-delay.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"constant","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SHIFT_TO_AVOID_ZERO","page":"Flight delay model","text":"Small positive shift added to the standard deviation of the departure/arrival intrinsic delay distributions, avoiding a degenerate zero-variance LogNormal/Normal distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SHIFT_TO_AVOID_ZERO"},{"category":"type","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCoefficients","page":"Flight delay model","text":"struct DelayCoefficients\n\nHandcrafted coefficients parameterizing the intrinsic (root) delay distributions of SyntheticDelayModel: one DelayEffects per weight vector of a HandcraftedDelayPredictor, a shared per-airport effect table, and the dynamic-simulator-only beta_* coefficients.\n\nThe beta_*_propagated, beta_dep_has_propagated and beta_arr_has_departure_delay coefficients are only used by the dynamic simulator (propagate_delays for SyntheticDelayModel), never by sample_root_scenarios. They default to 0.0, meaning the root delay model is purely static (route-independent). Setting them to nonzero values makes the resulting delays route-dependent, which is only valid for simulation, not as an input to stochastic_column_generation.\n\nFields\n\nmu_dep::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects: departure mu effects, pre-activation (log-minutes)\nsigma_dep::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects: departure sigma effects, pre-activation (log-minutes)\nmu_arr::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects: arrival mu effects (minutes)\nsigma_arr::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects: arrival sigma effects, pre-activation (minutes)\nairport_effects::Dict{String, Float64}: per-airport departure effect table (log-minutes, mean 0)\nairport_arr_target_sd::Float64: target standard deviation of the per-airport arrival effect table (minutes)\nbeta_dep_has_propagated::Float64: departure mu effect of a nonzero upstream propagated delay (dynamic simulator only)\nbeta_dep_propagated::Float64: departure mu effect of the upstream propagated delay value, per hour (dynamic simulator only)\nbeta_arr_has_departure_delay::Float64: arrival mu effect of a nonzero departure delay (dynamic simulator only)\nbeta_arr_propagated::Float64: arrival mu effect of the departure delay value, per hour (dynamic simulator only)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCoefficients"},{"category":"type","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects","page":"Flight delay model","text":"struct DelayEffects\n\nNamed per-leg effects making up one weight vector (mu_dep, sigma_dep, mu_arr or sigma_arr) of DelayCoefficients, all expressed relative to the population baseline of that component (base, or the tau/population_variance heterogeneity identity for the sigma components) and mean-centered by compile_weights so that they only redistribute delay across legs, without shifting the population mean.\n\nFields\n\nbase::Float64: population baseline of the component (component units, pre-activation for mudep and sigmadep/sigma_arr)\nhub::Float64: hub effect amplitude (component units)\nairport::Float64: own-airport effect amplitude, applied to the per-airport effect table (component units)\ncross_airport::Float64: other-airport (cross) effect amplitude, applied to the per-airport effect table (component units)\nhours::NTuple{5, Float64}: hour-of-day effect for the 00h-05h, 06h-09h, 10h-13h, 14h-17h and 18h-23h bands, in order (component units)\ndays::NTuple{7, Float64}: day-of-week effect, Monday to Sunday, in order (component units)\nduration::Float64: duration effect, per hour of deviation from a 5h reference duration (component units)\ntau::Float64: across-leg heterogeneity standard deviation of the mean, measured at risk_spread = 1 (component units, sigma components only)\npopulation_variance::Float64: population variance target used to re-derive the within-leg sigma base (component units squared, sigma components only)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects"},{"category":"type","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios","page":"Flight delay model","text":"struct DelayScenarios{T, R1, R2, F}\n\nPrecomputed standard normal scenarios for a given schedule, used through the reparameterization trick to sample intrinsic delays.\n\nFields\n\nschedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule: associated schedule to store scenarios on\ndeparture_scenarios::Matrix: matrix of precomputed standard normal draws for departure, size nb_legs x nb_scenarios\narrival_scenarios::Matrix: matrix of precomputed standard normal draws for arrival, size nb_legs x nb_scenarios\ndeparture_reparameterize::Any: method transforming a scenario draw and distribution parameters into a departure intrinsic delay\narrival_reparameterize::Any: method transforming a scenario draw and distribution parameters into an arrival intrinsic delay\nstatic_features::Any: static features (shared between departure and arrival), size nb_features x nb_legs\nfeature_names::Vector{String}: names of the static features (from the FeaturesConfig used to build the scenarios), used to check consistency against a SyntheticDelayModel's predictor\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"DelayScenarios(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    nb_scenarios,\n    departure_reparameterize,\n    arrival_reparameterize,\n    config,\n    seed\n) -> StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios{Float32, typeof(StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.lognormal_reparameterize), typeof(StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.normal_reparameterize), Matrix{Float32}}\n\n\nCustom constructor for DelayScenarios: draws nb_scenarios standard normal scenarios per leg of schedule, column by column, from two dedicated Random.Xoshiro random number generators, seeded respectively from hash((seed, :departure)) and hash((seed, :arrival)) (so that increasing nb_scenarios never changes the earlier columns, and so that the arrival stream of a given seed never collides with the departure stream of another seed), and computes the static features of every leg using config.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios"},{"category":"type","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor","page":"Flight delay model","text":"struct HandcraftedDelayPredictor\n\nLinear, handcrafted predictor for the intrinsic (root) delay distribution parameters (see departure_prediction and arrival_prediction), with weights compiled once from named, interpretable DelayCoefficients rather than learned.\n\nSince one-hot feature blocks always sum to 1 for a given leg, population baselines are injected as a uniform addition over the DayOfWeek one-hot block of the relevant weight vector (see compile_weights): this acts as an intercept without requiring a dedicated bias feature.\n\nFields\n\nw_mu_dep::Vector{Float32}: weight vector for the departure mu parameter, pre-activation\nw_sigma_dep::Vector{Float32}: weight vector for the departure sigma parameter, pre-activation\nw_mu_arr::Vector{Float32}: weight vector for the arrival mu parameter\nw_sigma_arr::Vector{Float32}: weight vector for the arrival sigma parameter, pre-activation\nfeature_names::Vector{String}: names of the static features, aligned with the weight vectors\ncoefficients::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCoefficients: coefficients used to compile the weight vectors\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCoefficients, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"HandcraftedDelayPredictor(\n    coefficients::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCoefficients,\n    config::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig;\n    risk_spread\n) -> StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor\n\n\nBuild a HandcraftedDelayPredictor from coefficients and config.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor"},{"category":"type","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel","page":"Flight delay model","text":"struct SyntheticDelayModel{P}\n\nSynthetic delay model: a HandcraftedDelayPredictor together with the shift, clamp and intensity parameters turning its LogNormal/Normal parameter predictions into intrinsic (root) departure and arrival delays.\n\nhas_dynamic_features reports whether any beta coefficient is nonzero, and if so only propagate_delays may be used.\n\nFields\n\npredictor::Any: predictor mapping static features to LogNormal/Normal distribution parameters\ndep_shift::Float64: positive shift of the root departure LogNormal (minutes)\narr_shift::Float64: positive shift of the root arrival Normal (minutes)\nmax_dep::Float64: maximum departure root delay allowed (minutes)\nmax_arr::Float64: maximum arrival root delay allowed (minutes)\ndelay_intensity::Float64: global multiplier applied to every root delay after shift and cap\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCostFunction-Union{Tuple{}, Tuple{T}} where T","page":"Flight delay model","text":"DelayCostFunction(; breakpoints, slopes)\n\n\nBuild a delay cost function from breakpoints and slopes, as a piecewise linear function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayCostFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.IdentityDelayCostFunction-Tuple{}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"Construct an identity delay cost function where the cost is equal to the delay.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.IdentityDelayCostFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._add_intercept!-Tuple{Vector{Float32}, Dict{String, Int64}, Any, Real}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_add_intercept!(\n    w::Vector{Float32},\n    index::Dict{String, Int64},\n    days,\n    value::Real\n) -> Vector{Float32}\n\n\nAdd value to every entry of the DayOfWeek one-hot block of w, indexed via index. Since exactly one such entry is active (equal to 1) for any leg, this acts as an intercept term.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._add_intercept!"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._airport_effect-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_airport_effect(\n    table::AbstractDict,\n    code::AbstractString\n) -> Any\n\n\nLook up the effect of code in table table, falling back to a small deterministic pseudo-random effect for code if absent, seeded from code itself so that it stays reproducible, bounded in [-0.025, 0.025], and with mean zero only in expectation over airport codes (not exactly zero for any given fallback code).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._airport_effect"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._airport_weights-Tuple{AbstractVector{String}}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_airport_weights(airports::AbstractVector{String}) -> Dict\n\n\nAssumed long-run per-airport usage weights (summing to 1) for airports (first(airports) is the hub, every other code an equally likely spoke), matching the stationary distribution of the random-walk instance generator (hub -> uniformly random spoke, spoke -> hub with probability DEFAULT_HUB_FRACTION, else another uniformly random spoke). Returns Dict(hub => 1.0) if airports has no spoke.\n\nUsed to center the per-airport and hub effects of DelayCoefficients so that they average out to 0 on a realistically hub-skewed schedule, rather than under a naive uniform-over-airports assumption.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._airport_weights"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._base_weight-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects, Real, Symbol}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_base_weight(\n    effects::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects,\n    risk_spread::Real,\n    component::Symbol\n) -> Any\n\n\nPopulation baseline (intercept, pre-activation) of one weight vector compiled by compile_weights for component (:mu_dep, :sigma_dep, :mu_arr or :sigma_arr).\n\nFor the two mu components, this is simply effects.base (risk_spread does not apply to the population baseline itself, only to the per-leg effects around it). For the two sigma components, effects.base is unused: the baseline is instead re-derived from the law-of-total-variance identity (risk_spread * effects.tau)^2 + sigma_base^2 + sigma_legs_variance = effects.population_variance (see _sigma_legs_variance), erroring out with a clear message if risk_spread is so large that the heterogeneity and sigma-variance terms alone would reach or exceed the population variance target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._base_weight"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._check_feature_layout-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_check_feature_layout(\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel\n)\n\n\nCheck that scenarios and model.predictor were built from the same FeaturesConfig (same feature names, in the same order), throwing a clear error otherwise.\n\nA mismatch (e.g. DelayScenarios built with the default airport list while model was built with schedule_airports(schedule), or the reverse) silently misaligns every feature-weight dot product, so this should always be checked before combining a DelayScenarios and a SyntheticDelayModel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._check_feature_layout"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._component_layout-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig, Symbol}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_component_layout(\n    config::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig,\n    component::Symbol\n) -> @NamedTuple{hour_prefix::String, hours::Vector{Int64}, airport_prefix::String, cross_prefix::String}\n\n\nFeature-name layout matching component (:mu_dep/:sigma_dep for the departure layout, :mu_arr/:sigma_arr for the mirrored arrival layout), used by compile_weights to look up the right one-hot blocks of config's feature vector: hour_prefix/hours for the own hour-of-day block, airport_prefix for the own airport block, cross_prefix for the other leg endpoint's airport block.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._component_layout"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._fill_onehot_mu!-Tuple{Vector{Float32}, Dict{String, Int64}, String, Any, Any, Real}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_fill_onehot_mu!(\n    w::Vector{Float32},\n    index::Dict{String, Int64},\n    prefix::String,\n    values,\n    effect_fn,\n    r::Real\n) -> Vector{Float32}\n\n\nWrite the mean-centered effect effect_fn.(values), scaled by risk_spread, into the one-hot block \"$prefix/$v\" of w for each v in values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._fill_onehot_mu!"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._rescale_to_sd-Tuple{AbstractDict, Real}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_rescale_to_sd(d::AbstractDict, target_sd::Real) -> Dict\n\n\nRescale every value of d so that the population standard deviation (no Bessel correction) of the values equals target_sd, preserving the mean (0 for our tables). Returns an all-zero dict if the population standard deviation of d is 0 (a constant table has no direction to rescale along).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._rescale_to_sd"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._sigma_legs_variance-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects, Real}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_sigma_legs_variance(\n    effects::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects,\n    risk_spread::Real\n) -> Any\n\n\nApproximate the across-leg variance of the (linearized) within-leg sigma induced by the hub and duration effects of effects, assuming the underlying features are mutually independent: the hub/spoke indicator (Bernoulli, mean POP_HUB_FREQUENCY) and the leg duration (standard deviation POP_DURATION_SD hours). Both effects are scaled by risk_spread, matching how they enter the weight vector in compile_weights.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._sigma_legs_variance"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._weighted_mean-Tuple{AbstractDict, Any, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"_weighted_mean(\n    weights::AbstractDict,\n    keys,\n    effect_fn\n) -> Any\n\n\nWeighted average of effect_fn.(keys) under weights.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel._weighted_mean"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.arrival_prediction-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"arrival_prediction(\n    p::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor,\n    x_arr;\n    mu_offset\n) -> NamedTuple{(:mu_arr, :sigma_arr), <:Tuple{Any, Any}}\n\n\nPredict the arrival intrinsic delay Normal parameters from static features x_arr.\n\nmu_offset is added to the mu_arr linear combination, used by propagate_delays to inject the dynamic (route-dependent) beta_arr_has_departure_delay/beta_arr_propagated effects without duplicating the weight dot product.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.arrival_prediction"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.compile_weights-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig, Symbol}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"compile_weights(\n    effects::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayEffects,\n    config::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig,\n    component::Symbol;\n    airport_effects,\n    risk_spread\n)\n\n\nCompile the weight vector for one component (:mu_dep, :sigma_dep, :mu_arr or :sigma_arr) of a HandcraftedDelayPredictor from effects and config, scaling every named per-leg effect of effects by risk_spread. airport_effects is the per-airport effect table read for both the own-airport and cross-airport (other leg endpoint) blocks.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.compile_weights"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.departure_prediction-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"departure_prediction(\n    p::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor,\n    x_dep;\n    mu_offset\n) -> NamedTuple{(:mu_dep, :sigma_dep), <:Tuple{Any, Any}}\n\n\nPredict the departure intrinsic delay LogNormal parameters from static features x_dep.\n\nmu_offset is added to the pre-activation mu_dep linear combination before the softplus, used by propagate_delays to inject the dynamic (route-dependent) beta_dep_has_propagated/beta_dep_propagated effects without duplicating the weight dot product.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.departure_prediction"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.feature_vector_arrival-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, Int64}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"feature_vector_arrival(\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    l::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the static feature vector associated to leg index l, for arrival.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.feature_vector_arrival"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.feature_vector_departure-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, Int64}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"feature_vector_departure(\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    l::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the static feature vector associated to leg index l, for departure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.feature_vector_departure"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.has_dynamic_features-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"has_dynamic_features(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel\n) -> Any\n\n\nCheck whether model uses dynamic (route-dependent) features, i.e. whether any of beta_dep_has_propagated, beta_dep_propagated, beta_arr_has_departure_delay, beta_arr_propagated in model.predictor.coefficients is nonzero (see SyntheticDelayModel and DelayCoefficients).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.has_dynamic_features"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.inv_softplus-Tuple{Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"inv_softplus(y) -> Any\n\n\nInverse of softplus, log(exp(y) - 1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.inv_softplus"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.lognormal_reparameterize-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"lognormal_reparameterize(\n    mu,\n    sigma,\n    scenario_value,\n    shift;\n    round_to_int\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the shifted, reparameterized intrinsic delay for scenario_value with a lognormal distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.lognormal_reparameterize"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.lognormal_reparameterize-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"lognormal_reparameterize(\n    mu,\n    sigma,\n    scenario_value;\n    round_to_int\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the reparameterized intrinsic delay for scenario_value with a lognormal distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.lognormal_reparameterize"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.normal_reparameterize-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"normal_reparameterize(\n    mu,\n    sigma,\n    scenario_value,\n    shift;\n    round_to_int\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the shifted, reparameterized intrinsic delay for scenario_value with a gaussian distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.normal_reparameterize"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.normal_reparameterize-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"normal_reparameterize(\n    mu,\n    sigma,\n    scenario_value;\n    round_to_int\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the reparameterized intrinsic delay for scenario_value with a gaussian distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.normal_reparameterize"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route, Int64}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"propagate_delays(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel,\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    route::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route,\n    s::Int64\n) -> @NamedTuple{departure_delays::Vector{Float32}, arrival_delays::Vector{Float32}, departure_root_delays::Vector{Float32}, arrival_root_delays::Vector{Float32}, propagated_delays::Vector{Float32}}\n\n\nSimulate a single scenario s of model on route, threading the upstream propagated delay through the dynamic (route-dependent) departure and arrival predictions (see DelayCoefficients.beta_dep_has_propagated and friends).\n\nReturns a named tuple (; departure_delays, arrival_delays, departure_root_delays, arrival_root_delays, propagated_delays), each a Vector{Float32} of length length(route) indexed by route position (maintenance positions hold the carried-over propagated delay, with a 0 intrinsic delay).\n\nwarning: Warning\nIf any beta_* coefficient of model.predictor.coefficients is nonzero, the resulting delays are route-dependent and must not be reused as input to stochastic_column_generation (unlike sample_root_scenarios).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"propagate_delays(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel,\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    routes::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}\n) -> @NamedTuple{departure_delays::Matrix{Float32}, arrival_delays::Matrix{Float32}, departure_root_delays::Matrix{Float32}, arrival_root_delays::Matrix{Float32}, propagated_delays::Matrix{Float32}}\n\n\nSimulate every scenario of model on routes, for every leg of scenarios's schedule (see propagate_delays for a single route and scenario).\n\nReturns a named tuple (; departure_delays, arrival_delays, departure_root_delays, arrival_root_delays, propagated_delays), each a nb_scenarios(scenarios) x nb_legs(scenarios) Matrix{Float32}, directly comparable to the output of propagate_delays_from_root_delays when every beta_* coefficient of model.predictor.coefficients is 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays_from_root_delays-Tuple{AbstractVector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, AbstractMatrix, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"propagate_delays_from_root_delays(\n    routes::AbstractVector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route},\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix,\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Matrix{Float32}\n\n\nPropagate input root_delays to compute delays for each leg in routes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays_from_root_delays"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays_from_root_delays-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route, AbstractMatrix, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"propagate_delays_from_root_delays(\n    route::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route,\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix,\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Matrix{Float32}\n\n\nPropagate input root_delays to compute delays for each leg in route.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.propagate_delays_from_root_delays"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenario-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, Int64}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"sample_root_scenario(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel,\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    leg_index::Int64\n) -> Vector\n\n\nSample the intrinsic (root) departure and arrival delays of leg leg_index, for every scenario in scenarios, as (eps_dep, eps_arr) pairs.\n\nwarning: Warning\nmodel should only use static features: has_dynamic_features(model) must be false. Dynamic (route-dependent) delay effects are only supported by propagate_delays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenario"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenario_sum-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios, Int64}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"sample_root_scenario_sum(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel,\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios,\n    leg_index::Int64\n) -> Vector\n\n\nSum of the departure and arrival intrinsic delays of leg leg_index, for every scenario in scenarios.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenario_sum"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenarios-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"sample_root_scenarios(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel,\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios\n) -> Any\n\n\nSample root delay scenarios for model and scenarios, summing departure and arrival intrinsic delays into a single value per leg and scenario.\n\nReturns a nb_scenarios(scenarios) x nb_legs(scenarios) Matrix{Float32}.\n\nwarning: Warning\nmodel should only use static features: see sample_root_scenario.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenarios"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenarios_unmerged-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel, StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"sample_root_scenarios_unmerged(\n    model::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel,\n    scenarios::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios\n) -> @NamedTuple{departure::Matrix{Float32}, arrival::Matrix{Float32}}\n\n\nSample root delay scenarios for model and scenarios, without summing the departure and arrival intrinsic delays.\n\nReturns a named tuple (; departure, arrival) of two nb_scenarios(scenarios) x nb_legs(scenarios) Matrix{Float32}.\n\nwarning: Warning\nmodel should only use static features: see sample_root_scenario.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.sample_root_scenarios_unmerged"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.softplus-Tuple{Any}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"softplus(x) -> Any\n\n\nNumerically stable softplus activation, log(1 + exp(x)).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.softplus"},{"category":"method","location":"91-api-delay/#StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.weight_table-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor}","page":"Flight delay model","text":"weight_table(\n    predictor::StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor\n) -> @NamedTuple{mu_dep::Vector{Pair{String, Float32}}, sigma_dep::Vector{Pair{String, Float32}}, mu_arr::Vector{Pair{String, Float32}}, sigma_arr::Vector{Pair{String, Float32}}}\n\n\nReturn feature_name => weight pairs for each of the 4 weight vectors of predictor, as a named tuple (; mu_dep, sigma_dep, mu_arr, sigma_arr).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.weight_table"},{"category":"section","location":"92-api-generator/#api-generator","page":"Instance generator","text":"Reference for the InstanceGenerator module, which builds synthetic benchmark instances (schedules, fleets and root delay scenarios) for the stochastic tail assignment problem.","title":"Instance generator"},{"category":"section","location":"92-api-generator/#Contents","page":"Instance generator","text":"Pages = [\"92-api-generator.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"92-api-generator/#Index","page":"Instance generator","text":"Pages = [\"92-api-generator.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator._generate_rotation!-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Instance generator","text":"_generate_rotation!(\n    legs,\n    leg_counter,\n    rng,\n    num_legs;\n    hub,\n    spokes,\n    spoke_distances,\n    hub_fraction,\n    horizon_start,\n    horizon_end,\n    horizon_minutes,\n    min_flight_duration,\n    max_flight_duration,\n    min_turn_time,\n    max_turn_time,\n    tight_turn_fraction,\n    aircraft_type\n)\n\n\nGenerate a single aircraft rotation (chain of legs starting and mostly returning to hub) in place into legs, stopping early (rather than skipping to a fresh hub departure) as soon as the next candidate leg would arrive after horizon_end.\n\nReturns the (airport, time) tail state of the rotation (last arrival airport and time) so that _pad_to_target! can later extend it, or nothing if no leg could be generated at all (e.g. the rotation's random start time leaves no room before the horizon).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator._generate_rotation!"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator._pad_to_target!-Tuple{Any, Any, Vector{Tuple{String, Dates.DateTime}}, Any, Any}","page":"Instance generator","text":"_pad_to_target!(\n    legs,\n    leg_counter,\n    rotation_tails::Vector{Tuple{String, Dates.DateTime}},\n    rng,\n    target;\n    hub,\n    spokes,\n    spoke_distances,\n    hub_fraction,\n    horizon_end,\n    min_flight_duration,\n    max_flight_duration,\n    min_turn_time,\n    max_turn_time,\n    tight_turn_fraction,\n    aircraft_type\n)\n\n\nPad legs up to target legs by appending legs to the tail of existing rotations (described by rotation_tails, a vector of (airport, time) states as returned by _generate_rotation!), instead of creating brand new hub departures that would require hidden extra aircraft.\n\nAt each step, the rotation with the earliest last arrival time is extended first (from its current airport, after a random turn time, to the hub or a spoke). A rotation that cannot take another leg before horizon_end is dropped from consideration. If no rotation can take more legs, padding stops early and length(legs) stays below target: callers must tolerate a leg count slightly below the requested one in that case.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator._pad_to_target!"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.build_delay_model-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Instance generator","text":"build_delay_model(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    coefficients,\n    delay_intensity,\n    risk_spread,\n    config\n) -> StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel{StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.HandcraftedDelayPredictor}\n\n\nBuild a SyntheticDelayModel for schedule, using a HandcraftedDelayPredictor compiled from coefficients (pass a custom per-airport effect table via coefficients=DelayCoefficients(; airport_effects=...)).\n\ndelay_intensity globally scales every intrinsic root delay after shift and cap (see SyntheticDelayModel). risk_spread scales every named per-leg effect of coefficients and re-derives the within-leg sigma so that the population-level delay distribution stays approximately unchanged while the spread of delay risk across legs increases (see DelayCoefficients).\n\nThe returned model is static-only (has_dynamic_features(model) == false), so it is a valid input to sample_root_scenarios and, through generate_root_delays, to stochastic_column_generation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.build_delay_model"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.default_nb_aircraft-Tuple{Int64}","page":"Instance generator","text":"default_nb_aircraft(nb_legs::Int64) -> Int64\n\n\nDefault nb_aircraft for a schedule with nb_legs legs, max(2, nb_legs ÷ 15), giving a legs-per-aircraft ratio of approximately 15, a ratio typical of short and medium haul operations, while ensuring feasibility across all instance sizes (50 to 600+ legs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.default_nb_aircraft"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_benchmark_instance-Tuple{Int64}","page":"Instance generator","text":"generate_benchmark_instance(\n    nb_legs::Int64;\n    nb_aircraft,\n    nb_extra_aircraft,\n    airports,\n    aircraft_type,\n    horizon_days,\n    nb_scenarios,\n    delay_intensity,\n    risk_spread,\n    delay_coefficients,\n    nb_seats,\n    seed,\n    delay_seed,\n    store_arc_index\n) -> Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule{MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph{Int64, Graphs.SimpleGraphs.SimpleDiGraph{Int64}, String, Vector{Float64}, Float64, String, MetaGraphsNext.var\"#MetaGraph##10#MetaGraph##11\", Float64}, G1, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg} where G1<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph, Any, PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction{Float64}}\n\n\nGenerate a complete benchmark instance ready for solving and evaluation.\n\nReturns (schedule, root_delays, delay_cost_function) where:\n\nschedule is an ActivitySchedule with nb_legs legs, or slightly fewer, see generate_legs\nroot_delays is an S x L Matrix{Float32} of root delays\ndelay_cost_function is a piecewise linear delay cost function (medium-haul slopes, weighted by nb_seats)\n\nThe default nb_aircraft is default_nb_aircraft(nb_legs), plus nb_extra_aircraft (only applied when nb_aircraft is not given explicitly).\n\nroot_delays is generated by generate_root_delays, forwarding delay_intensity, risk_spread and delay_coefficients (see build_delay_model and DelayCoefficients), with a delay seed of seed + 100 by default (override via delay_seed if a caller needs to reproduce this exact draw, e.g. to also sample the unmerged departure/arrival components with sample_root_scenarios_unmerged).\n\ndelay_cost_function uses the medium-haul slopes (FlightDelayModel.DELAY_COST_SLOPE_MEDIUM_HAUL) multiplied by nb_seats. Delay cost slopes are expressed per seat and per minute, and are scaled by the aircraft seat count. The default nb_seats=180 matches a typical narrow-body aircraft, nb_seats=1 recovers the unweighted (per-seat) slopes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_benchmark_instance"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_fleet-Tuple{}","page":"Instance generator","text":"generate_fleet(\n;\n    nb_aircraft,\n    aircraft_type,\n    fuel_factor_min,\n    fuel_factor_max,\n    seed\n)\n\n\nGenerate a vector of nb_aircraft random Immats of the given aircraft_type.\n\nFuel factors are drawn uniformly in [fuel_factor_min, fuel_factor_max]. Fuel factors are positive (typically 1.0 to 4.0), representing the percentage deviation from standard consumption.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_fleet"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_legs-Tuple{}","page":"Instance generator","text":"generate_legs(\n;\n    nb_legs,\n    airports,\n    nb_aircraft,\n    aircraft_type,\n    horizon_start,\n    horizon_days,\n    min_turn_time,\n    max_turn_time,\n    tight_turn_fraction,\n    min_flight_duration,\n    max_flight_duration,\n    hub_fraction,\n    seed\n)\n\n\nGenerate a vector of nb_legs random Legs with realistic airline structure.\n\nLegs are generated by simulating nb_aircraft aircraft performing rotations from a hub-and-spoke network. Each aircraft performs a variable number of legs (drawn from a Dirichlet-like distribution), creating realistic route length variability. The hub airport (first in airports) attracts most traffic via hub_fraction.\n\nFlight durations vary by destination distance: hub-spoke legs use the full duration range, while spoke-spoke legs use shorter durations.\n\nEach rotation stops as soon as its next leg would land after the horizon, and any shortfall is padded by extending the tail of existing rotations (never by creating new, disconnected hub departures). In the rare case where no rotation has room left before the horizon, padding stops early and the returned vector can have slightly fewer than nb_legs legs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_legs"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_root_delays-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Instance generator","text":"generate_root_delays(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    nb_scenarios,\n    seed,\n    delay_intensity,\n    risk_spread,\n    coefficients\n) -> Any\n\n\nGenerate an nb_scenarios x nb_legs(schedule) matrix of root delays (in minutes), compatible with propagate_delays_from_root_delays and full_cost(routes, root_delays, instance; delay_cost_function).\n\nDelays are generated from a SyntheticDelayModel (see build_delay_model): for each leg, the root delay in a given scenario is the sum of a departure intrinsic delay (LogNormal) and an arrival intrinsic delay (Normal), whose parameters depend on handcrafted, interpretable static features of the leg (hub/spoke airports, day of week, hour of day, duration). Negative root delays are not clamped to zero, since they represent early legs and are handled correctly by the delay propagation equations (they provide extra slack absorption).\n\nSee DelayCoefficients for the default model parameters, and delay_intensity/risk_spread in build_delay_model for the two global knobs exposed here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_root_delays"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_schedule-Tuple{}","page":"Instance generator","text":"generate_schedule(\n;\n    nb_legs,\n    nb_aircraft,\n    airports,\n    aircraft_type,\n    horizon_start,\n    horizon_days,\n    min_turn_time,\n    max_turn_time,\n    tight_turn_fraction,\n    min_flight_duration,\n    max_flight_duration,\n    hub_fraction,\n    fuel_factor_min,\n    fuel_factor_max,\n    standard_consumption,\n    TTM_factor,\n    seed,\n    store_arc_index\n)\n\n\nGenerate a full artificial ActivitySchedule, by generating nb_legs random legs (see generate_legs) and nb_aircraft random immatriculations (see generate_fleet), and combining them into an ActivitySchedule.\n\nThe legs are built from nb_aircraft rotations (see generate_legs), so the returned schedule is always coverable by its own fleet (see minimum_fleet_size for a standalone coverability check, used in tests).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.generate_schedule"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.minimum_fleet_size-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Instance generator","text":"minimum_fleet_size(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the minimum number of aircraft needed to cover all legs of schedule. See minimum_fleet_size(::Vector{<:AbstractLeg}).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.minimum_fleet_size"},{"category":"method","location":"92-api-generator/#StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.minimum_fleet_size-Tuple{Vector{<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg}}","page":"Instance generator","text":"minimum_fleet_size(\n    legs::Vector{<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg};\n    TTM_factor\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the minimum number of aircraft needed to cover all of legs, i.e. the minimum path cover of the leg chaining DAG (an edge u -> v exists whenever v could immediately follow u on the same aircraft, per is_valid_chaining).\n\nBy König's theorem, the minimum path cover of a DAG equals the number of vertices minus the size of a maximum matching of the bipartite graph obtained by splitting each vertex into an \"out\" and an \"in\" copy. The matching is computed with a simple Kuhn augmenting-path algorithm, which is fast enough for the instance sizes generated here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.InstanceGenerator.minimum_fleet_size"},{"category":"section","location":"93-api-colgen/#api-colgen","page":"Column generation","text":"Reference for the top-level StochasticTailAssignment module, which implements the deterministic MIP, the stochastic column generation pricing algorithm and the diving heuristic.","title":"Column generation"},{"category":"section","location":"93-api-colgen/#Contents","page":"Column generation","text":"Pages = [\"93-api-colgen.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"93-api-colgen/#Index","page":"Column generation","text":"Pages = [\"93-api-colgen.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"type","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource","page":"Column generation","text":"struct BackwardResource{P<:PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction}\n\nFields\n\ng::Vector{P} where P<:PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction: one piecewise linear function per scenario, computing the associated partial path delay cost.\noperational_cost_sum::Float64: accumulates sum of operational costs\nλ_sum::Float64: accumulated sum of dual variables along the associated partial path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource"},{"category":"type","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.ForwardExtensionFunction","page":"Column generation","text":"struct ForwardExtensionFunction\n\nData structures defining the forward extension functions for the column generation algorithm. It lives on the arcs of the graph. It is used to expand resources at the tail of arcs (see TailForwardResource). The considered node index of the arc is stored in the field activity_index.\n\nFields\n\noperational_cost::Float64: leg cost of node + chaining cost\nλ::Float64: dual variable λ of node\nroot_delays::Vector{Float64}: root delay of node for each scenario\nslack_with_turn_time::Float64: slack (with turn time) between the two activities of the arc\nactivity_index::Int64: activity index of node\nis_tail_maintenance::Bool: true if tail of arc is a maintenance activity (or dummy), used for knowing when not to compute delay costs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.ForwardExtensionFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.ForwardExtensionFunction-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"Extend the forward resource r with the tail forward extension function f.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.ForwardExtensionFunction"},{"category":"type","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource","page":"Column generation","text":"struct PartialBackwardResource\n\nFields\n\noperational_cost_sum::Float64: accumulates sum of operational costs\nλ_sum::Float64: accumulated sum of dual variables along the associated partial path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource"},{"category":"type","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.TailBackwardExtensionFunction","page":"Column generation","text":"struct TailBackwardExtensionFunction\n\nData structures defining the backward extension functions for the column generation algorithm. It lives on the arcs of the graph.\n\nFIELDS\n\nroot_delays::Vector{Float64}: root delay for each scenario of the arc tail\nslack_with_turn_time::Float64: slack between the two activities of the arc\noperational_cost::Float64: operational cost of the arc tail + chaining cost\nλ::Float64: dual variable λ of the arc tail\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.TailBackwardExtensionFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.TailBackwardExtensionFunction-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"Extend the backward resource r with the tail backward extension function f.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.TailBackwardExtensionFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.TailBackwardExtensionFunction-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"Extend the backward resource r with the tail backward extension function f.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.TailBackwardExtensionFunction"},{"category":"type","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource","page":"Column generation","text":"struct TailForwardResource <: StochasticTailAssignment.AbstractForwardResource\n\nForward resource structure for the column generation algorithm, expanded from the tail.\n\nFields\n\noperational_cost_sum::Float64: accumulated sum of operational costs\ndelay_cost_sum::Float64: accumulated delay cost\nλ_sum::Float64: accumulated sum of dual variables\npropagated_delay::Vector{Float64}: propagated delay before the current node of the forward path\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#Base.:<=-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource, StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"<=(\n    r₁::StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource,\n    r₂::StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if forward resource r₁ dominates forward resource r₂.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.:<="},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#Base.min-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource, StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"min(\n    r1::StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource,\n    r2::StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource\n) -> StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource\n\n\nCompute the meet between two backward resource.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.min"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#Base.min-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource, StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"min(\n    r1::StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource,\n    r2::StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource\n) -> StochasticTailAssignment.PartialBackwardResource\n\n\nCompute the meet between two partial backward resource.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.min"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.backward_tail_shortest_path-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Int64, AbstractVector, AbstractMatrix, Vararg{Any, 5}}","page":"Column generation","text":"backward_tail_shortest_path(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    immat_index::Int64,\n    λ_val::AbstractVector,\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix,\n    partial_bounds,\n    current_bounds,\n    FF,\n    BF,\n    order;\n    delay_cost_function\n)\n\n\nSolve the pricing problem for aircraft immat_index and dual variable values λ_val. Uses a resource constrained shortest path enumeration algorithm with bounding.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.backward_tail_shortest_path"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.build_stochastic_model-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, AbstractMatrix, PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction}","page":"Column generation","text":"build_stochastic_model(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix,\n    delay_cost_function::PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction;\n    model_builder,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    silent,\n    time_limit,\n    warm_start_routes\n) -> JuMP.Model\n\n\nBuild JuMP model for solve_stochastic_aircraft_routing_mip.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.build_stochastic_model"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.compute_partial_bounds-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, AbstractMatrix, Int64}","page":"Column generation","text":"compute_partial_bounds(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix,\n    immat_index::Int64;\n    delay_cost_function\n)\n\n\nPrecompute partial bounds for aircraft immat_index.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.compute_partial_bounds"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.compute_partial_bounds-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, AbstractMatrix}","page":"Column generation","text":"compute_partial_bounds(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix;\n    delay_cost_function\n)\n\n\nPrecompute partial bounds for each aircraft.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.compute_partial_bounds"},{"category":"function","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.diving_heuristic_with_backtracking!","page":"Column generation","text":"diving_heuristic_with_backtracking!(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    columns,\n    root_delays,\n    dual_values;\n    ...\n)\ndiving_heuristic_with_backtracking!(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    columns,\n    root_delays,\n    dual_values,\n    max_discrepancy;\n    ...\n)\ndiving_heuristic_with_backtracking!(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    columns,\n    root_delays,\n    dual_values,\n    max_discrepancy,\n    taboo_list;\n    ...\n)\ndiving_heuristic_with_backtracking!(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    columns,\n    root_delays,\n    dual_values,\n    max_discrepancy,\n    taboo_list,\n    partial_solution;\n    model_builder,\n    delay_cost_function,\n    depth,\n    silent,\n    tol\n)\n\n\nDiving heuristic with backtracking, maintaining a taboo_list of columns excluded from selection, and backtracking up to max_discrepancy times when column generation becomes infeasible after fixing a column into partial_solution.\n\nReturns (solution, feasible), where feasible indicates whether a feasible integer solution was found.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.diving_heuristic_with_backtracking!"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.encode_routes_to_solution-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Column generation","text":"encode_routes_to_solution(\n    routes,\n    instance\n) -> Array{Int64, 3}\n\n\nEncode input routes to a MIP solution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.encode_routes_to_solution"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.filter_proper_columns!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Column generation","text":"filter_proper_columns!(mask, columns, route)\n\n\nRemove all columns that are incompatible with the given route being in the the solution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.filter_proper_columns!"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.forward_tail_shortest_path-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Int64, AbstractVector, AbstractMatrix}","page":"Column generation","text":"forward_tail_shortest_path(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    immat_index::Int64,\n    λ_val::AbstractVector,\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix;\n    delay_cost_function\n)\n\n\nSolve the pricing problem for aircraft immat_index and dual variable values λ_val. Uses a resource constrained shortest path enumeration algorithm.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.forward_tail_shortest_path"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.partial_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"partial_cost(\n    r::StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource\n) -> Float64\n\n\nComputes the cost of the partial path corresponding to the input forward resource.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.partial_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.pure_diving_heuristic-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Column generation","text":"pure_diving_heuristic(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    columns,\n    root_delays,\n    dual_values;\n    model_builder,\n    delay_cost_function,\n    silent\n)\n\n\nApply a (pure) diving heuristic to the instance, using the given columns and scenarios.\n\nArguments\n\ninstance::Instance: the instance to solve\ncolumns: output of the column generation\nroot_delays: root delay scenarios\ndual_values: dual variable values at the end of the column generation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.pure_diving_heuristic"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.retrieve_relaxation_solution_from_columns_and_duals-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Any, Any}","page":"Column generation","text":"retrieve_relaxation_solution_from_columns_and_duals(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    columns,\n    dual_values\n) -> Vector{Float64}\n\n\nCompute compact primal relaxation solution from columns and duals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.retrieve_relaxation_solution_from_columns_and_duals"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.solve_stochastic_aircraft_routing_mip-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Any, PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction}","page":"Column generation","text":"solve_stochastic_aircraft_routing_mip(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    root_delays,\n    delay_cost_function::PiecewiseLinearFunctions.PiecewiseLinearFunction;\n    silent,\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{NamedTuple{(:routes, :obj, :status, :time, :gap), <:Tuple{Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, Union{Float64, Vector{Float64}}, MathOptInterface.TerminationStatusCode, Any, Float64}}, NamedTuple{(:routes, :obj, :status, :time, :gap), <:Tuple{Vector{Vector{Int64}}, Float64, MathOptInterface.TerminationStatusCode, Any, Float64}}}\n\n\nSolve the stochastic tail assignment problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.solve_stochastic_aircraft_routing_mip"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.stochastic_column_generation-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}}","page":"Column generation","text":"stochastic_column_generation(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    initial_paths::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route};\n    model_builder,\n    root_delays,\n    delay_cost_function,\n    max_nb_columns,\n    tol,\n    silent,\n    backward,\n    add_all_columns,\n    starting_sweep\n)\n\n\nPerform column generation to solve the stochastic tail assignment problem.\n\nArguments\n\ninstance: an instance of AbstractSchedule (also works with MaskedSchedule)\ninitial_paths: initial paths to start the column generation, should at least include one path per aircraft\nmodel_builder: function to build the JuMP model\nroot_delays: root_delays[s, l] is the delay of leg l in scenario s\ndelay_cost_function: function mapping delays to costs\nmax_nb_columns: maximum number of columns to generate\ntol: tolerance for reduced cost\nsilent: whether to print information\n\nReturns:\n\ncolumns: vector of generated columns as a Vector{Route}\nmodel: final JuMP model\nVV: reduced cost evolution for each aircraft\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.stochastic_column_generation"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.stochastic_column_heuristic-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, AbstractMatrix}","page":"Column generation","text":"stochastic_column_heuristic(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    columns::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route},\n    root_delays::AbstractMatrix;\n    model_builder,\n    silent,\n    delay_cost_function,\n    bin,\n    time_limit,\n    warm_start\n)\n\n\nTake a vector of Routes and return the solution of the restricted master problem heuristic for the stochastic tail assignment problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.stochastic_column_heuristic"},{"category":"method","location":"93-api-colgen/#StochasticTailAssignment.stochastic_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource, StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource}","page":"Column generation","text":"stochastic_cost(\n    rf::StochasticTailAssignment.TailForwardResource,\n    rb::StochasticTailAssignment.BackwardResource\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the cost of combining tail forward path with backward path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.stochastic_cost"},{"category":"section","location":"94-api-learning/#api-learning","page":"Learning","text":"Reference for the Learning module, which generates imitation learning datasets and trains the statistical pricing model.","title":"Learning"},{"category":"section","location":"94-api-learning/#Contents","page":"Learning","text":"Pages = [\"94-api-learning.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"94-api-learning/#Index","page":"Learning","text":"Pages = [\"94-api-learning.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.build_loss-Tuple{}","page":"Learning","text":"build_loss(\n;\n    ε,\n    nb_samples,\n    model_builder\n) -> NamedTuple{(:loss, :maximizer), <:Tuple{Union{InferOpt.FenchelYoungLoss{InferOpt.PerturbedOracle{InferOpt.AdditivePerturbation{Distributions.Normal{Float64}}, InferOpt.LinearMaximizer{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#9\"{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#8#10\"{typeof(StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.highs_model)}}, StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#g#13\"{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#g#12#14\"}, ComposedFunction{typeof(zero), typeof(InferOpt.eltype_kw)}}, false, true, Nothing, Random.TaskLocalRNG, Nothing}}, InferOpt.FenchelYoungLoss{O} where O<:(InferOpt.PerturbedOracle{InferOpt.AdditivePerturbation{Distributions.Normal{Float64}}, InferOpt.LinearMaximizer{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#9\"{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#8#10\"{typeof(StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.highs_model)}}, StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#g#13\"{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#g#12#14\"}, ComposedFunction{typeof(zero), typeof(InferOpt.eltype_kw)}}, _A, _B, InferOpt.NormalAdditiveGradLogdensity, Random.TaskLocalRNG, Nothing} where {_A, _B})}, StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#9\"{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#8#10\"{typeof(StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.highs_model)}}}}\n\n\nBuild the Fenchel-Young loss (with a PerturbedAdditive optimization layer) used to train the pricing model by imitation of the diving heuristic's expert solutions.\n\nReturns a NamedTuple with fields loss (the FenchelYoungLoss) and maximizer (the raw combinatorial oracle, see build_maximizer).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.build_loss"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.build_maximizer-Tuple{}","page":"Learning","text":"build_maximizer(\n;\n    model_builder\n) -> StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#9\"{StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.var\"#maximizer#8#10\"{typeof(StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.highs_model)}}\n\n\nBuild the combinatorial optimization maximizer used as the pricing oracle in the InferOpt pipeline.\n\nThe returned function takes the predicted edge weights θ (one per interior arc) and solves the edge-based MIP (see aircraft_routing_edge_maximizer) to return the corresponding arc solution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.build_maximizer"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.compute_features-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, AbstractMatrix, AbstractMatrix}","page":"Learning","text":"compute_features(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    departure_root_delays::AbstractMatrix,\n    arrival_root_delays::AbstractMatrix\n) -> Matrix{Float32}\n\n\nCompute learning features for each interior arc (arc not connected to the source s nor the sink t) of instance, using the unmerged root delay scenarios departure_root_delays and arrival_root_delays.\n\ndeparture_root_delays and arrival_root_delays are S x L matrices (S scenarios, L legs), as produced by sample_root_scenarios_unmerged (their sum matches the merged root_delays used for the expert labels and evaluation, see generate_dataset). Column j of each matrix corresponds to instance.legs[j] (for an ActivitySchedule, leg vertex indices are exactly 1:nb_legs(instance), so a leg vertex v is also its own column index).\n\nFor each interior arc (u, v, i), the following 23 features are computed, following the slack definition of the delay-model-informed features (the downstream leg v's intrinsic delay only affects its own departure, while the upstream leg u contributes its arrival intrinsic delay):\n\nω, the slack between u and v (1 value)\nω_tt, the slack between u and v including the minimum turn time (1 value)\nquantiles_with, the 0.1:0.1:1.0 quantiles of the slack scenarios ω_tt - eps_arr(u) + eps_dep(v), accounting for the departure intrinsic delay of v (10 values)\nquantiles_without, the 0.1:0.1:1.0 quantiles of the slack scenarios ω_tt - eps_arr(u), without accounting for the departure intrinsic delay of v (10 values)\ncost, the edge cost of (u, v, i) (1 value)\n\nReturns a Matrix{Float32} of size (23, nb_interior_arcs(instance)), where column arc_index[u, v, i] holds the features of arc (u, v, i).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.compute_features"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.compute_normalization-Tuple{Any}","page":"Learning","text":"compute_normalization(\n    data\n) -> NamedTuple{(:mins, :ranges), <:Tuple{Any, Any}}\n\n\nCompute per-feature normalization statistics (mins, ranges) over the feature matrices of data, as produced by generate_dataset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.compute_normalization"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.default_model-Tuple{Any}","page":"Learning","text":"default_model(nb_features; hidden_dims) -> Flux.Chain\n\n\nBuild a default feedforward neural network mapping nb_features input features to a single scalar edge weight per arc, with hidden layers of dimensions hidden_dims.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.default_model"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.evaluate_metrics-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Learning","text":"evaluate_metrics(\n    data,\n    model,\n    maximizer\n) -> NamedTuple{(:operational_cost_gap, :delay_cost_gap, :full_cost_gap, :avg_time), <:NTuple{4, Any}}\n\n\nEvaluate model on data (as produced by generate_dataset) by comparing the routes it induces (through maximizer) to the expert routes, in terms of relative operational cost gap, delay cost gap and full cost gap, along with the average solving time of maximizer.\n\nCosts are computed on eval_root_delays, a held-out scenario set distinct from the root_delays used to build the features and expert labels (see generate_dataset), so that the gap reflects out-of-sample quality.\n\nEach gap is only accumulated over the instances where the corresponding expert cost is strictly positive, and averaged over that same count of instances (not over length(data)), so that instances with a zero expert cost (e.g. no delay cost at all) do not silently dilute the average. Because of this, the returned gaps are not comparable to a mean computed over all instances of data. avg_time, on the other hand, is averaged over all instances of data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.evaluate_metrics"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.generate_dataset-Tuple{Int64}","page":"Learning","text":"generate_dataset(\n    nb_instances::Int64;\n    nb_legs,\n    nb_scenarios,\n    nb_eval_scenarios,\n    nb_feature_scenarios,\n    seed,\n    silent,\n    relaxation,\n    model_builder,\n    max_nb_columns,\n    tol,\n    time_limit,\n    risk_spread,\n    delay_intensity,\n    nb_seats,\n    nb_extra_aircraft,\n    max_discrepancy,\n    kwargs...\n) -> Vector\n\n\nGenerate a learning dataset of nb_instances labeled examples for the stochastic tail assignment pricing problem.\n\nEach instance is generated with generate_benchmark_instance (with store_arc_index=true), solved to (near-)optimality with the deterministic MIP followed by the stochastic column generation and diving heuristic, and labeled with the resulting expert routes.\n\nIf relaxation is true, the expert arc labels ȳ are the LP relaxation arc marginals returned by the column generation (for training with relaxation=true in train_model!). If relaxation is false (the default), ȳ is the binary arc solution decoded from the diving heuristic routes. In both cases, routes is always computed via the diving heuristic (needed for evaluation/baseline).\n\nBoth expert labels are always computed and returned regardless of relaxation, so that a single dataset can be reused to train against either target: ȳ_integer is the binary arc solution decoded from the diving heuristic routes (target D^Y), and ȳ_relaxation is the fractional arc-incidence vector of the column generation relaxation, a convex combination of columns with entries in [0, 1] (target D^Ỹ). Both share the same arc indexing as ȳ and as the edge MIP maximizer (see aircraft_routing_edge_maximizer).\n\nroot_delays is the scenario matrix used to build the features x and to solve for the expert labels (routes, ȳ_integer, ȳ_relaxation). eval_root_delays is a second, held-out nb_eval_scenarios x nb_legs root delay matrix for the same schedule, sampled independently (with a seed offset by 10_000 from root_delays's), meant to be used for evaluation (see evaluate_metrics) instead of the training scenarios.\n\ndeparture_root_delays and arrival_root_delays are the unmerged departure and arrival components of root_delays (see sample_root_scenarios_unmerged), sampled from the same StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.SyntheticDelayModel and the same delay seed as root_delays (so that departure_root_delays .+ arrival_root_delays == root_delays), and passed to compute_features to build x. If nb_feature_scenarios differs from nb_scenarios, departure_root_delays and arrival_root_delays are instead drawn from a separate, unmerged scenario set of size nb_feature_scenarios (same delay model, seed offset by 20_000 from the delay seed), used only to compute x, not for root_delays or the expert labels. A larger nb_feature_scenarios gives smoother slack quantile features, at the cost of extra sampling.\n\nReturns a Vector of NamedTuples with fields instance, x (features), ȳ (expert arc solution selected by relaxation), ȳ_integer, ȳ_relaxation, routes (expert routes, from the diving heuristic), root_delays, departure_root_delays, arrival_root_delays, eval_root_delays, delay_cost_function, expert_time (wall-clock time of the stochastic column generation plus diving heuristic call only, excluding instance generation and the deterministic MIP warm start, suitable for a fair \"expert solving time\" comparison).\n\nrisk_spread, delay_intensity, nb_seats and nb_extra_aircraft are forwarded to generate_benchmark_instance.\n\nmax_discrepancy is the taboo list size limit forwarded to diving_heuristic_with_backtracking!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.generate_dataset"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.normalize_data-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Learning","text":"normalize_data(data, dt) -> Any\n\n\nNormalize the feature matrices of data using the normalization statistics dt computed by compute_normalization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.normalize_data"},{"category":"method","location":"94-api-learning/#StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.train_model!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Learning","text":"train_model!(\n    model,\n    fyl_loss,\n    maximizer,\n    data_train,\n    data_val;\n    nb_epochs,\n    relaxation\n) -> NamedTuple{(:loss_history, :metrics_train, :metrics_val, :best_model, :best_epoch), <:Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Vector{NamedTuple}, Vector{NamedTuple}, Any, Int64}}\n\n\nTrain model by imitation of the expert solutions in data_train, using the Fenchel-Young loss fyl_loss (see build_loss) and evaluating with maximizer on data_train and data_val after each epoch.\n\nAt each epoch (including epoch 0, before any update), the validation full cost gap (metrics_val[epoch].full_cost_gap) is compared to the best value seen so far, and a deepcopy of model is checkpointed whenever it improves.\n\nReturns a NamedTuple with fields loss_history, metrics_train, metrics_val, best_model (a deepcopy of model at the epoch with the lowest validation full cost gap) and best_epoch (that epoch number, 0 meaning before any training step).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.Learning.train_model!"},{"category":"section","location":"90-api-routing/#api-routing","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Reference for the AircraftRoutingBase module, which defines the core aircraft routing entities (legs, aircraft, activity schedules) and static leg features.","title":"Aircraft routing base"},{"category":"section","location":"90-api-routing/#Contents","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Pages = [\"90-api-routing.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"90-api-routing/#Index","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Pages = [\"90-api-routing.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"constant","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.DEFAULT_AIRPORT_SIZE","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Fallback airport size used for airports not present in DEFAULT_AIRPORT_SIZES (or in a custom airport_sizes dictionary).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.DEFAULT_AIRPORT_SIZE"},{"category":"constant","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.DEFAULT_AIRPORT_SIZES","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Default per-airport size lookup, in [0, 1], for the synthetic airport codes used by the instance generator (HUB is the hub, A to G are spokes).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.DEFAULT_AIRPORT_SIZES"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"abstract type AbstractActivity\n\nAbstract type defining an activity.\n\nTwo implementations\n\nLeg\nMaintenance\n\nCommon methods\n\nis_maintenance\nstart_airport\nend_airport\nstart_time\nend_time\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"abstract type AbstractLeg <: StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n\nAbstract type defining a leg\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractRoute","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"abstract type AbstractRoute\n\nAbstract type for a route.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractRoute"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"abstract type AbstractSchedule\n\nData structure defining a schedule of activities. Two implementations :\n\nActivitySchedule : the main data structure, containing all the information about the schedule.\nMaskedSchedule : a masked version of the ActivitySchedule, where some activities are removed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct ActivitySchedule{G<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph, G1<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph, L<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg, A} <: StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n\nData structure defining a schedule of activities. It corresponds to an instance of the aircraft routing (fleet assignment) problem.\n\nFields\n\nimmats::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Immat}: all available immatriculations\nlegs::Vector{L} where L<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg: all legs that need to be operated in the schedule\nmaintenances::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}: all maintenance task that need to be performed in the schedule\nforced_chainings::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ForcedChaining}: all forced chaining enforced in the schedule\ngraph::MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph: dependency (acyclic) digraph between activities\nimmat_graphs::Vector{G1} where G1<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph: specialized digraph for each immatriculation, removing useless edges\nTTM_factor::Float64: minimum turn time multiplier that was used to compute graph edges\ninclude_chaining_costs::Bool: whether to include chaining costs in the operational costs\narc_index::Any: [u, v, i] = arc index for learning\nnb_interior_arcs::Int64: number of (u, v, i) not connected to s or t\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule-Tuple{}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"ActivitySchedule(\n;\n    immats,\n    legs,\n    maintenances,\n    forced_chainings,\n    fuel_cost_per_kg,\n    standard_consumption,\n    tractage_cost,\n    empty_graph,\n    TTM_factor,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    store_arc_index,\n    sparsification_threshold\n)\n\n\nConstructor for an ActivitySchedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct FeaturesConfig{A}\n\nConfiguration for computing static leg features.\n\nThis does not carry any min-max scaling information, the handcrafted delay model works directly on the raw, unscaled feature values.\n\nFields\n\nairports::Vector{String}: list of available airports (categories other than these are grouped as other)\ndays::Vector{Int64}: list of all possible days of week (1 = Monday, ..., 7 = Sunday)\nstart_hours::Vector{Int64}: list of all possible departure hours\nend_hours::Vector{Int64}: list of all possible arrival hours\nairport_sizes::Any: store info about airport sizes, in [0, 1]\nnames::Vector{String}: list of feature names (output of compute_leg_feature_names)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ForcedChaining","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct ForcedChaining\n\nData structure defining an forced chaining between two activities.\n\nFields\n\nfirst_activity_id::String: id of the first activity\nsecond_activity_id::String: id of the second activity chained to the first one\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ForcedChaining"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Immat","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct Immat\n\nData structure defining an aircraft immatriculation.\n\nFields\n\nid::String: unique identifier string\nfuel_factor::Float64: fuel factor, the percentage of extra fuel consumption for the aircraft type\nlast_activity_id::String: id of the last activity operated by this immatriculation\naircraft_type::String: aircraft type code of the immatriculation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Immat"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct Leg <: StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg\n\nFields\n\nid::String: Unique identifier\ndeparture_airport::String: IATA code of the departure airport\narrival_airport::String: IATA code of the arrival airport\ndeparture_time::Dates.DateTime: departure time in UTC\narrival_time::Dates.DateTime: arrival time in UTC\naircraft_type::String: aircraft type code\nminimum_turn_time::Int64: minimum rurn time in minutes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct Maintenance <: StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n\nFields\n\nid::String: unique identifier\nlocation::String: IATA code of the airport\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime: start time of the maintenance in UTC\nend_time::Dates.DateTime: end time of the maintenance in UTC\nimmat::String: immat code of the aircraft conserned by the maintenance\nminimum_turn_time::Int64: minimum turn time in minutes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.MaskedSchedule","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct MaskedSchedule{T<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, G<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph, G1<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph} <: StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n\nWrapper over ActivitySchedule to represent a schedule where some routes are fixed. For each route, the associared immat does not need to be considered anymore, as well as the activities in the route.\n\nFields\n\nschedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule: associated schedule\nimmat_mask::BitVector: mask of immats that are not fixed\nactivity_mask::BitVector: mask of activities that are not fixed\nleg_mask::Any: mask of legs that are not fixed\ngraph::MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph: connection graph\nimmat_graphs::Vector{G1} where G1<:MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph: connection sub graphs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.MaskedSchedule"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct PartialRoute\n\nThis data structure enables defining a partial route with a time window. This is used to split a route between maintenances, to only consider legs.\n\nFields\n\nleg_route::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route: list of leg indices corresponding to this partial route\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime: start of the time window for this partial route\nend_time::Dates.DateTime: end of the time window for this partial route\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute"},{"category":"type","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.RouteWithMaintenance","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"struct RouteWithMaintenance <: StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractRoute\n\nRoute data structure with useful maintenance information.\n\nFields\n\nroute::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route: a route containing only leg indices\nmaintenances::Vector{Vector{Int64}}: for each leg in route, ordered list of maintenance indices before the next leg\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.RouteWithMaintenance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#Dates.dayofweek-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"dayofweek(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the day of week of activity start time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Dates.dayofweek"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#Dates.month-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"month(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the month of activity start time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Dates.month"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.activity_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Any, Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"activity_cost(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    v,\n    i\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the cost of operating activity (usually a leg) corresponding to index v with aircraft immatriculation (index) i in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.activity_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.activity_indices-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"activity_indices(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> UnitRange{Int64}\n\n\nRetrieve all activity indices in the schedule. Useful for iteration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.activity_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.aircraft_routing_edge_maximizer-Tuple{AbstractVector}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"aircraft_routing_edge_maximizer(\n    θ::AbstractVector;\n    instance,\n    verbose,\n    kwargs...\n)\n\n\nCO layer for the aircraft routing problem with edge-based MIP model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.aircraft_routing_edge_maximizer"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.aircraft_type-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"aircraft_type(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> String\n\n\nReturns the aircraft type of the first leg in the schedule, assuming all legs have the same aircraft type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.aircraft_type"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.aircraft_type-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"aircraft_type(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the aircraft type of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.aircraft_type"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"arrival_airport(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the arrival airport of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_airport"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_airport_size-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, Dict}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"arrival_airport_size(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    airport_size_dict::Dict\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the arrival airport size for given activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_airport_size"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_hour","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Alias for end_hour.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_hour"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"arrival_time(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nRetrieve the arrival time of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.arrival_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.build_immat_graphs-Tuple{MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Immat}, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}, Vector{<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg}}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"build_immat_graphs(\n    graph::MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph,\n    immats::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Immat},\n    maintenances::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance},\n    legs::Vector{<:StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg};\n    empty_graph\n) -> Vector\n\n\nBuild a subgraph for each immatriculation, corresponding to the routing graph for that immatriculation. Use the same base graph for all immat graphs, in order to have the same vertex indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.build_immat_graphs"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.build_model-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"build_model(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule;\n    model_builder,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    silent,\n    feasibility_only,\n    relaxation,\n    time_limit\n) -> JuMP.Model\n\n\nBuild the MIP model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.build_model"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.build_model_θ_edge-Tuple{AbstractVector, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"build_model_θ_edge(\n    θ::AbstractVector,\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    model_builder,\n    silent,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    use_operational_costs,\n    relaxation\n) -> JuMP.Model\n\n\nBuild the MIP model with θ as cost weights in the objective.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.build_model_θ_edge"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.chaining_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"chaining_cost(\n    ::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    ::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity;\n    tractage_cost\n) -> Float64\n\n\nReturn the chaining cost between two successive activities.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.chaining_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.chaining_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"chaining_cost(\n    previous_leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg,\n    next_leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg;\n    tractage_cost\n) -> Float64\n\n\nReturn the chaining cost between two successive legs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.chaining_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.chaining_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Any, Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"chaining_cost(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    u,\n    v\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve (from the graph) the cost of chaining from vertex u to vertex v.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.chaining_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.column_generation-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"column_generation(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    initial_paths::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route};\n    model_builder,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    max_iterations,\n    tol,\n    silent\n) -> Tuple{Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, JuMP.Model, Vector{Vector{Float64}}}\n\n\nPerform column generation to solve the deterministic tail assignment problem.\n\nReturns:\n\ncolumns: vector of generated columns as a Vector{Route}\nmodel: final JuMP model\nVV: reduced cost evolution for each aircraft\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.column_generation"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.column_heuristic-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"column_heuristic(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    columns::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route};\n    model_builder,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    silent,\n    bin,\n    column_cost,\n    time_limit,\n    warm_start\n) -> Tuple{Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, Union{Float64, Vector{Float64}}}\n\n\nTake a vector of Routes and returns the solution of the restricted master problem heuristic for the deterministic tail assignment problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.column_heuristic"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_arc_index-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_arc_index(\n    immat_graphs,\n    graph\n) -> Tuple{Dict{Tuple{Int64, Int64, Int64}, Int64}, Int64}\n\n\nCompute the arc index for the given graph and schedule. [u, v, i] -> arc index\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_arc_index"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_arc_index-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_arc_index(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n) -> Tuple{Dict{Tuple{Int64, Int64, Int64}, Int64}, Int64}\n\n\nCompute the arc index for the given schedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_arc_index"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_edge_mask-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_edge_mask(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Any\n\n\nReturns a boolean mask of the edges that connect two activity (i.e. neither of the dummy vertices).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_edge_mask"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_feature_info-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_feature_info(\n    config::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.FeaturesConfig\n) -> @NamedTuple{names::Vector{String}, index::Dict{String, Int64}}\n\n\nCompute lookup information associated to config: the feature names, and a name => index dictionary giving the position of each named feature in the vectors returned by compute_leg_features.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_feature_info"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_leg_feature_names-Tuple{}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_leg_feature_names(\n;\n    airports,\n    days,\n    start_hours,\n    end_hours\n)\n\n\nCompute the static feature names, in the same order as compute_leg_features.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_leg_feature_names"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_leg_features-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_leg_features(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity;\n    airports,\n    days,\n    start_hours,\n    end_hours,\n    airport_sizes,\n    type\n)\n\n\nCompute the static features of the input activity, using the given configuration.\n\nLet A = length(airports) and C = A + 1 (the airport categories, plus the other category). Concatenate the following features, in order:\n\nminimum turn time, in hours\nduration of the leg, in hours\n\n3-9. one-hot encoding of the day of week (7 values) 10-33. one-hot encoding of the departure hour (24 values) 34-57. one-hot encoding of the arrival hour (24 values) 58 to (57 + C). one-hot encoding of the departure airport, including an other category (C values) (58 + C) to (57 + 2C). one-hot encoding of the arrival airport, including an other category (C values) (58 + 2C). airport size of the departure airport, in [0, 1] (59 + 2C). flight distance proxy, clamp(duration_hours / 10, 0, 1) (60 + 2C). haul type, 1 if the leg duration is more than 240 minutes, 0 otherwise\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_leg_features"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_shortest_route-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Int64, Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_shortest_route(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    immat_index::Int64,\n    λ_val;\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    silent\n)\n\n\nSolve the pricing problem for given aircraft immat_index and dual variables λ_val. This is solved as successive shortest paths between scheduled maintenances for immat_index.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_shortest_route"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_shortest_subpath-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"compute_shortest_subpath(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    start_node,\n    end_node,\n    weights\n) -> Vector\n\n\nCompute a shortest path between start_node and end_node, with weight matrix weights. Uses the ford bellman algorithm, since the graph is acyclic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.compute_shortest_subpath"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_arc_solution_from_routes-Tuple{Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"decode_arc_solution_from_routes(\n    routes::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route},\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    type\n) -> Any\n\n\nRecompute binary variables solution of the MIP model from given routes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_arc_solution_from_routes"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_routes_from_arc_solution-Tuple{Any, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"decode_routes_from_arc_solution(\n    y_val,\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}\n\n\nDecode routes from the binary variables of the solution of the MIP model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_routes_from_arc_solution"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_routes_from_solution-Tuple{Any, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"decode_routes_from_solution(\n    y_val,\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n) -> Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}\n\n\nDecode routes from the binary variables of the solution of the MIP model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_routes_from_solution"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_solution_from_routes-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"decode_solution_from_routes(\n    routes,\n    instance\n) -> Union{Array{Float64, 3}, Matrix}\n\n\nRecompute binary variables solution of the MIP model from given routes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.decode_solution_from_routes"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"departure_airport(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the departure airport of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_airport"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_airport_size-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, Dict}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"departure_airport_size(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    airport_size_dict::Dict\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the departure airport size for given activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_airport_size"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_hour","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Alias for start_hour.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_hour"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"departure_time(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nRetrieve the departure time of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.departure_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.duration-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"duration(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Float64\n\n\nCompute the duration of an activity in minutes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.duration"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.edge_cost-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Int64, Int64, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"edge_cost(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    u::Int64,\n    v::Int64,\n    i::Int64;\n    include_chaining_costs\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the cost of an edge as the sum of the operational cost of the destination plus the eventual chaining cost of the edge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.edge_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.edge_cost_origin-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Int64, Int64, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"edge_cost_origin(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    u::Int64,\n    v::Int64,\n    i::Int64;\n    include_chaining_costs\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the cost of an edge as the sum of the operational cost of the origin plus the chaining cost of the edge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.edge_cost_origin"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"end_airport(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the end airport of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_airport"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"end_airport(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the location of given maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_airport"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_hour-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"end_hour(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the hour of activity start time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_hour"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"end_time(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nRetrieve the arrival time of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"end_time(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nRetrieve the end time of given maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.end_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.flight_distance-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg, Dict}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"flight_distance(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg,\n    distance_dict::Dict\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the flight distance for given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.flight_distance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.flight_distance-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance, Dict}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"flight_distance(\n    _::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance,\n    _::Dict\n) -> Float64\n\n\nRetrieve the flight distance for given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.flight_distance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_activity-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_activity(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    activity_index::Int64\n) -> Union{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}\n\n\nRetrieve the activity corresponding to the given index.\n\nwarning: Warning\nThis method might be type instable. It can return either a Leg or a Maintenance, depending on activity_index value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_activity"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_last_activity_index-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_last_activity_index(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    immat_index::Int64\n) -> Integer\n\n\nReturn last activity index of immat if it exists, else index of s.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_last_activity_index"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_maintenance_indices-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_maintenance_indices(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    immat_index::Int64;\n    sorted\n) -> Vector{Int64}\n\n\nReturn a vector of node indices corresponding to all maintenances affected to aircraft immat_index. Sorted by start time by default.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_maintenance_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_s-Tuple{MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_s(graph::MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph) -> Integer\n\n\nRetrieve the vertex code of the source vertex s in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_s"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_s-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_s(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n) -> Integer\n\n\nRetrieve the vertex code of the source vertex s in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_s"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_t-Tuple{MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_t(graph::MetaGraphsNext.MetaGraph) -> Integer\n\n\nRetrieve the vertex code of the sink vertex t in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_t"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_t-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"get_t(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n) -> Integer\n\n\nRetrieve the vertex code of the sink vertex t in the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.get_t"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.highs_model-Tuple{}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"highs_model() -> JuMP.Model\n\n\nInitialize a HiGHS model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.highs_model"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.id-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"id(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Any\n\n\nRetrieve the id of given activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.id"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.immat-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"immat(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the immat code associated to given maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.immat"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.immat_indices-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"immat_indices(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> UnitRange{Int64}\n\n\nRetrieve all immatriculation indices in the schedule. Useful for iteration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.immat_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_dummy_vertex-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_dummy_vertex(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    activity_index::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nCheck if activity_index is either one of the two dummy vertices of the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_dummy_vertex"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_feasible-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_feasible(\n    route::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route,\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    verbose\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if a given route is feasible.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_feasible"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_feasible-Tuple{Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_feasible(\n    routes::Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route},\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    verbose\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if routes are feasible.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_feasible"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_intersection-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_intersection(\n    p1::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute,\n    p2::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if two partial routes intersect in time, i.e. if they are elegible for a swap.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_intersection"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_leg-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_leg(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    activity_index::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nCheck if given activity index activity_index corresponds to a leg activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_leg"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_location_compatible-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_location_compatible(\n    previous_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    next_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if two successive activities are location compatible, i.e. if the arrival airport of previous_activity is the departure airport of next_activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_location_compatible"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_maintenance-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_maintenance(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule,\n    activity_index::Int64;\n    safe_mode\n) -> Any\n\n\nCheck if given activity index activity_index corresponds to a maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_maintenance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_maintenance-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_maintenance(\n    _::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if an activity is a maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_maintenance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_maintenance-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_maintenance(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if an activity is a maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_maintenance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_s-Tuple{Any, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_s(schedule, activity_index::Int64) -> Any\n\n\nCheck if activity_index is the source of the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_s"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_t-Tuple{Any, Int64}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_t(schedule, activity_index::Int64) -> Any\n\n\nCheck if activity_index is the sink of the graph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_t"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_time_compatible-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_time_compatible(\n    previous_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    next_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity;\n    TTM_factor\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if two successive activities are time compatible, i.e. if the slack between them is larger than the minimumturntime of next_activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_time_compatible"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_time_compatible-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_time_compatible(\n    previous_maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance,\n    next_maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance;\n    TTM_factor\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if two successive maintenances are time compatible.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_time_compatible"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_valid_chaining-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"is_valid_chaining(\n    previous_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    next_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity;\n    verbose,\n    TTM_factor\n) -> Bool\n\n\nCheck if a given activity chaining (two successive activities) are compatible. Additionaly prints a warning if the chaining is not compatible and verbose is true.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.is_valid_chaining"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.leg_airport_size-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, AbstractDict}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"leg_airport_size(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    airport_sizes::AbstractDict\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the airport size of the departure airport of leg, defaulting to DEFAULT_AIRPORT_SIZE for airports not present in airport_sizes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.leg_airport_size"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.leg_indices-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"leg_indices(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> UnitRange{Int64}\n\n\nRetrieve all leg indices in the schedule. Useful for iteration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.leg_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.leg_indices_from_route-Tuple{Any, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"leg_indices_from_route(\n    route,\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule\n) -> Vector\n\n\nReturns an ordered vector of leg activity indices in route (i.e. filtering out maintenances).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.leg_indices_from_route"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.mask_graph!-Tuple{Any, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"mask_graph!(\n    graph,\n    route::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route;\n    verbose\n)\n\n\nRemove edges connected to masked activities (this allows keeping consistent vertex indexing)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.mask_graph!"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.minimum_turn_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"minimum_turn_time(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Float64\n\n\nRetrieve the minimum turn time for an activity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.minimum_turn_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.minimum_turn_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"minimum_turn_time(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> Float64\n\n\nRetrieve the minimum turn time of given maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.minimum_turn_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_activities-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"nb_activities(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the total number of activities (legs + maintenances) in the schedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_activities"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_immats-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"nb_immats(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the number of immatriculations in the schedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_immats"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_legs-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"nb_legs(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the number of legs in the schedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_legs"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_maintenances-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"nb_maintenances(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the number of maintenances in the schedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.nb_maintenances"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_aircraft_type-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg, AbstractVector}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_aircraft_type(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractLeg,\n    aircraft_types::AbstractVector\n) -> Vector{Bool}\n\n\nEncode the aircraft type of given leg as a one-hot vector.\n\naircraft_types should the list of all possible aircraft types. If the activity type is not in the list, it is encoded as the \"other\" category.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_aircraft_type"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_arrival_airport","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Alias for onehot_end_airport.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_arrival_airport"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_arrival_hour","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Alias for onehot_end_hour.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_arrival_hour"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_dayofweek","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_dayofweek(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Vector{Bool}\nonehot_dayofweek(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    range\n) -> Vector{Bool}\n\n\nEncode the day of week of given activity as a one-hot vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_dayofweek"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_departure_airport","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Alias for onehot_start_airport.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_departure_airport"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_departure_hour","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"Alias for onehot_start_hour.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_departure_hour"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_end_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, AbstractVector}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_end_airport(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    airports::AbstractVector\n) -> OneHotArrays.OneHotVector{UInt32}\n\n\nEncode the end airport of given activity as a one-hot vector.\n\nairports should the list of all possible airports. If the activity airport is not in the list, it is encoded as the \"other\" category.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_end_airport"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_end_hour","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_end_hour(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Vector{Bool}\nonehot_end_hour(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    range\n) -> Vector{Bool}\n\n\nEncode the and hour of given activity as a one-hot vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_end_hour"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_month","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_month(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Vector{Bool}\nonehot_month(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    range\n) -> Vector{Bool}\n\n\nEncode the start month of given activity as a one-hot vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_month"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_start_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, AbstractVector}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_start_airport(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    airports::AbstractVector\n) -> OneHotArrays.OneHotVector{UInt32}\n\n\nEncode the start airport of given activity as a one-hot vector.\n\nairports should the list of all possible airports. If the activity airport is not in the list, it is encoded as the \"other\" category.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_start_airport"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_start_hour","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"onehot_start_hour(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Vector{Bool}\nonehot_start_hour(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    range\n) -> Vector{Bool}\n\n\nEncode the start hour of given activity as a one-hot vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.onehot_start_hour"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.operational_cost-Tuple{Vector{Vector{Int64}}, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"operational_cost(\n    routes::Vector{Vector{Int64}},\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule;\n    include_chaining_costs\n) -> Any\n\n\nCompute the total cost of operating all activities in the routes routes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.operational_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.read_instance-Tuple{Any}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"read_instance(\n    path;\n    standard_consumption,\n    TTM_factor,\n    include_chaining_costs,\n    kwargs...\n)\n\n\nRead instance from custom json data format at path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.read_instance"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.route_to_partial_routes-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"route_to_partial_routes(\n    route::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route,\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.PartialRoute}\n\n\nConvert a given feasible route into a vector of partial routes splitting the maintenances.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.route_to_partial_routes"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.schedule_airports-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"schedule_airports(\n    schedule::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n) -> Vector{String}\n\n\nList the airports used by schedule, ordered by decreasing usage (as either departure or arrival airport), so that first(...) is the busiest one (the hub, for a schedule generated by generate_schedule). Airports with equal usage counts are ordered alphabetically, so the result is a deterministic total order.\n\nUsed to build a FeaturesConfig that matches the airport codes actually present in schedule, rather than assuming the [\"HUB\", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\", \"F\", \"G\"] default, which only matches generate_schedule's own default when explicitly requested (e.g. via generate_benchmark_instance).\n\nDefined here (rather than in InstanceGenerator) so that both FlightDelayModel (default config of StochasticTailAssignment.FlightDelayModel.DelayScenarios) and InstanceGenerator (default config of build_delay_model) can build a matching, consistent FeaturesConfig without a circular dependency.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.schedule_airports"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.scip_model-Tuple{}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"scip_model() -> JuMP.Model\n\n\nInitialize a SCIP model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.scip_model"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.slack-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"slack(\n    previous_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    next_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Float64\n\n\nReturn the slack time between two successive activities.\n\nwarning: Warning\nThis does not include the minimum turn time. For that, use slack_with_turn_time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.slack"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.slack_with_turn_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity, StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"slack_with_turn_time(\n    previous_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity,\n    next_activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Float64\n\n\nReturn the slack time between two successive activities, including the minimum turn time of the second activity. slack(l₁, l₂) = (scheduled duration between arrival of l1 and departure of l2) - (minimum turn time)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.slack_with_turn_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.solve_aircraft_routing-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"solve_aircraft_routing(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractSchedule;\n    relaxation,\n    silent,\n    time_limit,\n    kwargs...\n) -> Tuple{Union{Nothing, Vector{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Route}, Vector{Vector{Int64}}}, Union{Float64, Int64, Vector{Float64}}, Any}\n\n\nSolve the aircraft routing problem using a MIP solver. Returns the routes and objective value of the best solution found.\n\nIf a time limit is hit before a feasible incumbent is found (primal_status(model) != MOI.FEASIBLE_POINT), warns and returns the sentinel (Vector{Int}[], -1, nothing). If a feasible incumbent exists but the solver did not prove optimality, warns and still decodes and returns that (possibly suboptimal) incumbent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.solve_aircraft_routing"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"start_airport(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the start airport of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_airport"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_airport-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"start_airport(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> String\n\n\nRetrieve the location of given maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_airport"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_hour-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"start_hour(\n    activity::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.AbstractActivity\n) -> Int64\n\n\nRetrieve the hour of activity start time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_hour"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"start_time(\n    leg::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Leg\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nRetrieve the departure time of given leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_time"},{"category":"method","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_time-Tuple{StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance}","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"start_time(\n    maintenance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.Maintenance\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nRetrieve the start time of given maintenance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.start_time"},{"category":"function","location":"90-api-routing/#StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.write_instance","page":"Aircraft routing base","text":"write_instance(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule\n)\nwrite_instance(\n    instance::StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.ActivitySchedule,\n    path\n)\n\n\nWrite given input schedule to custom json data format at path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StochasticTailAssignment.AircraftRoutingBase.write_instance"},{"category":"section","location":"#StochasticTailAssignment","page":"StochasticTailAssignment","text":"Documentation for StochasticTailAssignment.","title":"StochasticTailAssignment"}]
